{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516057-dark-ages-v20-bloodline-ganolentii","id":1516057,"title":"[Dark Ages V20] Bloodline: Ganolentii","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-24T20:59:00-07:00","id":1516057,"title":"[Dark Ages V20] Bloodline: Ganolentii","content":"Ok, another bloodline but this time built around the concepts of carrion and violence.<br /> <br /> <b>Ganolentii</b> (Sing. Ganolentis) - Yes, my language skills are very bad but I hope no one will tear their eyes out.<br /> <br /> Coming from ancient times the Carrions have stalked, or made, sites of violence for many thousands of nights. While some find them useful due to their hardiness many more are disgusted with them or see them as threats to the Cainite society due to their enforced lack of discretion in feeding practices. The Galoentii themselves tell a tale of a curse from the heavens which brought a new curse on them beyond the curse of vampirism. For what crime, dishonor or sin they were cursed no one knows but many belives one thing or another. Pushed into the margins of Cainite society they make do with other Low Clans and outcasts who will stomach them. They seem to have a particular hostility from Cainites on the Road of Humanity and so most of the Carrions eschew that Road and its Paths. Instead the Roads of Sin and Heaven are more favored. Sin to embrace their stigma and Heaven to seek either forgviness or give their existance a purpose.<br /> <br /> Historically the bloodshed of the ancient and medieval worlds would offer sufficient feeding for this bloodline to make it through those nights but with the formation of the Camarilla and the adoption of Humanity the Carrions had their fate sealed of the few that the Inquisition had not claimed. A few are rumored to have joined with the Sabbat to escape Camarilla persecution but nothing is confirmed.<br /> <br /> <b>Sobrique:</b> Carrions<br /> <br /> <b>Appearence:</b> They tend to wear only practical clothing, or torn cloths stolen from the dead, for a hard unlife on the road and a unlife filled with strife.<br /> <br /> <b>Haven:</b> Havens are varied according to personal staste and resources but is most often Laconic in its simplicity and with many instruments of violence found within. For any Ganolentis knows that although hardy they face many threats and more than a few have embraced a violent way of unlife with scant regards for the prey they must feed on or the many forces of the world who would put them down.<br /> <br /> <b>Embrace:</b> Due to the need to drain a prospective Childer of blood the Embrace is a horrific experience of pain and fear. Many do not survive the damage inflicted on their bodies in the process and and survivers often carry scars from this event for the rest of their existance.<br /> <br /> <b>Disicplines:</b> Potence, Auspex, Fortitude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Ganolentii cannot drink blood through their fangs. While they can administer the Kiss to their victim they must in the end drink blood in the same fashion as a human would, opening a sufficiently large and deep wound through other means and then drink their fill. This naturally makes the act of feeding most often a far more violent act than many other Cainites face and often leaves the victim dead or in shock afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Small bands of Ganolentii can be found trailing after armies or haunting places of war or banditry as many find it easier to descend on the freshly dead or dying to feast on their blood in a place where to find violently slain bodies. This banding together also gives them common defence against outsiders who take offence at their feeding needs. Thus a lone Ganolentis is a rare thing to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","use